  "title": "Resistivity and D.C. circuits",
  "main_stem": null,
  "parts": [
    {
      "label": "(a)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "A metal wire has a resistance per unit length of $0.92\\,\\Omega\\,\\mathrm{m}^{-1}$. The wire has a uniform cross-sectional area of $5.3 \\times 10^{-7}\\,\\mathrm{m}^2$. Calculate the resistivity of the metal of the wire.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(i)",
      "part_stem": "A battery of electromotive force (e.m.f.) $E$ and negligible internal resistance is connected in series with a fixed resistor and a light-dependent resistor (LDR), as shown in Fig. 6.1. [Fig. 6.1 shows a series loop containing battery $E$, $1400\\,\\Omega$ fixed resistor and $1600\\,\\Omega$ LDR, with a voltmeter $V$ connected across the LDR.] The resistance of the fixed resistor is $1400\\,\\Omega$. The intensity of the light illuminating the LDR causes it to have a resistance of $1600\\,\\Omega$. A voltmeter connected across the LDR reads $6.4\\,\\mathrm{V}$.",
      "text": "Show that the current in the LDR is $4.0 \\times 10^{-3}\\,\\mathrm{A}$.",
      "marks": 1,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(ii)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "Calculate the number of free electrons passing through the LDR in a time of 3.2 minutes.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(iii)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "Calculate the e.m.f. $E$.",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(iv)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "Determine the ratio $$\\frac{\\text{power dissipated in LDR}}{\\text{power dissipated in fixed resistor}}.$$",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)(i)",
      "part_stem": "The environmental conditions change causing a decrease in the resistance of the LDR in (b). The temperature of the environment does not change. State whether there is a decrease, increase or no change to:",
      "text": "the intensity of the light illuminating the LDR",
      "marks": 1,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)(ii)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "the current in the battery",
      "marks": 1,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)(iii)",
      "part_stem": null,
      "text": "the reading of the voltmeter.",
      "marks": 1,
      "answer_prompt": null,
      "unit": null
    }
  ],
  "markscheme": [
    {
      "label": "(a)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "$R = \\rho L / A$"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "$\\rho = 0.92 \\times 5.3 \\times 10^{-7}$ $= 4.9 \\times 10^{-7}\\,\\Omega\\,\\mathrm{m}$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(i)",
      "marks": 1,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "(current =) $6.4 / 1600 = 4.0 \\times 10^{-3}$ (A)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(ii)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "charge $= 4.0 \\times 10^{-3} \\times 3.2 \\times 60$ ($= 0.768\\,\\mathrm{C}$)"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "number $= 0.768 / 1.6 \\times 10^{-19}$ $= 4.8 \\times 10^{18}$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(iii)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "$6.4 / E = 1600 / (1400 + 1600)$ or $E = 6.4 + (4.0 \\times 10^{-3} \\times 1400)$ or $E = 4.0 \\times 10^{-3} (1600 + 1400)$"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "$E = 12\\,\\mathrm{V}$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(b)(iv)",
      "marks": 2,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "C1",
          "text": "$P = I^2 R$ or $P = VI$ or $P = V^2 / R$"
        },
        {
          "tag": "A1",
          "text": "ratio $= (6.4^2 / 1600) / [(4.0 \\times 10^{-3})^2 \\times 1400]$ $= 1.1$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)(i)",
      "marks": 1,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "B1",
          "text": "increase"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "(c)(ii)",
      "marks": 1,
      "marking_points": [
        {
          "tag": "B1",
          "text": "increase"
        }
